   },
   "block_C_100_101": {
    "n": 2,
    "with_fractional_windows": 0,
    "with_decay_linear": 0,
    "with_IndClass": 1,
    "mean_chars": 171
   },
   "fractional_part_mean": 0.517,
   "fractional_part_n": 174,
   "verdict": "Alphas 1-57 carry ZERO fractional windows; 40 of 42 alphas in 58-99 carry them, with fractional parts ~uniform on [0,1) (mean 0.517, n=174). Block B is also 1.7x longer, 9x more decay_linear and 16x more IndClass. The published library is a hand-built corpus and a machine-generated corpus fused into one flat list of 101; the paper never says so."
  },
  "F6_indneutralize_is_not_group_zscore_MT5_measured": {
   "spec": "Canonical indneutralize(x,g) = cross-sectional DEMEAN within group. The desk's libs/alpha_factory/wq_operators.py exposes group_rank and group_zscore only; group_zscore demeans THEN divides by the within-group cross-sectional sd. There is no demean-only operator, so the desk cannot express indneutralize -- the operator that 18 of the 101 canonical alphas call, and the exact 18 that s11's grouping map was built to unblock.",
   "measurement": {
    "panel": "52 Fusion symbols with >=70% daily coverage, D1 from the desk's own _H1 parquets, 2021-01-04..2026-08-26, 1454 bars, 1449 days measured",
    "groups": {
     "Forex": 21,
     "Crypto": 14,
     "Forex Exotics": 9,
     "Commodities": 5,
     "Indices": 3
    },
    "grouping_map": "data/mt5_grouping_map.json asset_class arm (s11)",
    "signal_neutralized": "5-day mean of daily log return",
    "daily_cross_sectional_spearman_demean_vs_group_zscore": {
     "mean": 0.914,
     "p05": 0.857,
     "p25": 0.895,
     "frac_below_0.90": 0.293
    },
    "median_within_group_cross_sectional_sd": {
     "Forex": 0.00172,
     "Forex Exotics": 0.00193,
     "Indices": 0.00237,
     "Commodities": 0.0025,
     "Crypto": 0.01063
    },
    "max_min_group_sd_ratio": 6.2
   },
   "mechanism": "Dividing by within-group sd rescales each group by a DIFFERENT constant, so the interleaving of groups in the pooled cross-section changes. Because within-group dispersion spans 6.2x on this book (Forex 0.00172 -> Crypto 0.01063), group_zscore systematically amplifies the lowest-dispersion group and suppresses the highest. On the paper's own venue (US equities) within-sector dispersion is broadly comparable across sectors, so the substitution is nearly harmless THERE and is not on a multi-asset CFD book. This is a venue-specific failure of an equity-venue operator assumption.",
   "verdict": "Two distinct operators, ~29% of days disagree materially, and the desk has only the wrong one. Same class and comparable magnitude to s12's corr/cov find (0.920).",
   "population_stated": "52 of 251 registry symbols. The known partial parquet sync limits the panel; an earlier attempt over the full 1970-2026 span produced a spurious Spearman of exactly 1.000 because only ONE group (Crypto, 14 symbols) populated any given day. That artifact is recorded here so it is not re-derived."
  }
